      <span style="background: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.12); color: #f59e0b; border: 1px solid rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.35); padding: 4px 14px; border-radius: 20px; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 14px;">STEP-BY-STEP PROCESS</span>
      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Step-by-Step Moving Day Workflow: Survey, Packing, Transit &amp; Placement for packers and movers in shillong</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>Before any boxes are sealed, the first step in a smooth relocation in Shillong is a thorough pre‑move assessment. A professional team will conduct a video walk‑through from a mobile device, followed by a detailed on‑site survey.</p>
<p>This dual‑approach captures the layout, identifies fragile items, notes door widths, stairwell heights, and gauges the distance from the loading dock to the destination. The video provides a reference for the client and the movers, while the physical survey allows the crew to mark each room and create a custom packing plan.</p>

<p>The packing phase follows a strict room‑by‑room protocol. Each space is tagged, and items are sorted into categories: fragile, valuable, bulky, and miscellaneous. The crew uses high‑quality packing materials—reinforced boxes, bubble wrap, packing paper, and stretch film—to secure every piece.</p>
<p>A colour‑coded system (red for fragile, blue for valuables, green for general) helps avoid mix‑ups. The packing manager reviews the inventory list against the client’s checklist, ensuring nothing is left behind.</p>

